            <ArticleTitle>TGF-beta-mediated control of allergen-specific T-cell responses.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>259-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Control of allergen-specific response by suppressive cytokines involves several layers of regulation, including secretion of the cytokine, deviation of cytokine expression by altered T-cell differentiation, immediate (de-) phosphorylation events upon binding of suppressive cytokines, and laterations in susceptibility of suppression.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
